onfigure Google Tag Manager, primary use Google Analytics\n- - Basic Cookie Consent Banner to allow tracking, follow best practices for ethical use\n- - Consent banner should be centered for mobile, off to the left side for tablet and above\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nThe (AI)lephant in the Room\n\nArtificial Intelligence tools have made the last two years the most transformational period for web development since the rise of the smartphone. There's a lot of noise around it, mostly from the heavily vested, but in my experience I have have found these things to be true:\n1. The tools are getting faster and smarter, but they are not infallible\n2. They are becoming as indispensible for business as the telephone or internet\n2. There will always be room for the human element\nIn my own practice, I have found that while these tools are good for building components and elements quickly, they aren't quite there yet for the full engine. It's the intersection of design and code, overlaid with the interface of ideas and execution. \n\n\n\n\n\n// blog idea -- not related -- persistence of concepts (XML->Flash JS->Everything, pop-ups to keep folks \"on the page\", perfectly centered & perfect @ 640x480)\n\n// blog idea - Bottom Line, Every Time - how failure to secure the paperwork soured the relationships\n\n// blog idea - Cultural Drift, I'm a PNW Cat, East Coast types are difficult",
